<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture is Chicago95's status/audio-volume-high.png
     (architect 2026-10-05, the icon pass's caption pick — the same 16-px
     file the caption wears at a bitmap gui_scale, icons.h's AppIcon head),
     scaled NEAREST-NEIGHBOUR (the Chicago95 artwork is period-pixel art, so
     no smoothing) and centred on a transparent canvas: no plate, no sheet
     grey, the icon's own transparent corners carrying through. An ADAPTIVE
     icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so no legacy ic_launcher.png set
     exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH generated from
     the one source (assets/icons/chicago95/16/audio-volume-high.png):
       ic_launcher_background.png  fully transparent, the canvas size alone;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the 16-px icon scaled by an integer
                                   factor k with CAIRO_FILTER_NEAREST's ImageMagick
                                   equivalent (-filter point), centred on a
                                   transparent canvas of the density's full
                                   108 dp.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art must sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner zone, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. k = 4 puts the scaled icon at 64 dp square (16 * 4), just inside
     that zone, the same k at every density (the per-density PNG pixel size
     scales with the density factor f alone, never with k):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  icon 64f  offset (C-64f)/2  resize factor
       mdpi     1    108            64        22                 400% (k=4)
       hdpi     1.5  162            96        33                 600% (k=6)
       xhdpi    2    216            128       44                 800% (k=8)
       xxhdpi   3    324            192       66                 1200% (k=12)
       xxxhdpi  4    432            256       88                 1600% (k=16)

     (The per-density ImageMagick resize factor is k*100 scaled by f again,
     since -resize's percentage multiplies the 16 px source directly to the
     density's own pixel count — 400% * f, e.g. 1600% at xxxhdpi for the same
     64 dp.) THE RECIPE, from the repo root (ImageMagick 7), for each
     density's resize percentage P and canvas C above:

       magick assets/icons/chicago95/16/audio-volume-high.png \
           -filter point -resize P% -background none -gravity center \
           -extent CxC -strip -define png:compression-level=9 \
           -define png:compression-filter=5 \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-<density>/ic_launcher_foreground.png
       magick -size CxC xc:none -strip \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-<density>/ic_launcher_background.png

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop
     and committed; a retouch is a re-run of this recipe, never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). The Linux desktop's launcher icon
     (packaging/warptempo_gui.svg, the .desktop's Icon=) is the same picture,
     one rect per pixel, written by tools/desktop_icon/gen_desktop_icon.py. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
